      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've been experiencing this issue, and it has gotten progressively worse over the past few days.  Its now at the point where my mic input dies within *minutes* of a new session.\nUnfortunately, I only have one audio input device, so I cannot switch back and forth to workaround the issue.\nEDIT: Like a lot of issues I've had in VRChat, this seems to be connected with the cache growing too large.  The issue has apparently gone away or is taking longer to manifest after I cleared my downloaded content cache, which previously was at least 11gb.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-09T01:05:37.497Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As title says, the microphone stops working after a while and requires me to switch to another input device and then back to my primary microphone to get working again. When this happens, the following events are logged to the output_log file:\n\n2019.10.09 02:48:59 Log        -  [USpeaker] uSpeak [1][1365953679]: playback buffer FULL (length: 10), clearing playback buffer\n2019.10.09 02:48:59 Log        -  [USpeaker] uSpeak [1][1365953680](every 10): voice buffer underrun, sample arrived 0ms late\n2019.10.09 02:49:28 Log        -  [USpeaker] uSpeak [1][1365982495]: playback buffer FULL (length: 10), clearing playback buffer\n2019.10.09 02:49:28 Log        -  [USpeaker] uSpeak [1][1365982495](every 10): voice buffer underrun, sample arrived 0ms late\n2019.10.09 02:49:33 Log        -  [USpeaker] uSpeak [1][1365986986]: Segment playback time didn't match audio data length, audio cpu usage may be too high! - playbackTimeMS/audioLengthMS: 4271/2900",
